\paragraph{Simulation only.} All results are simulated; a real-robot validation is needed to confirm that internalized collision awareness survives the sim-to-real gap.

\paragraph{Binary collision definition.} SafeLIBERO defines collision as binary contact (any contact constitutes a collision). For tasks requiring push-through-obstacle motions or compliant contact, the collision penalty may over-suppress necessary interactions---a general limitation of collision-free safety paradigms. Future work could address this via task-conditioned safety margins or force-aware collision thresholds.

